//
// Version: 0.12.1
//
// `huginn local on` follows the device-enrolment grammar exactly: consent →
// fetch pinned → validate → install → enrol. This file is the manager the shell
// wrapper hands over to; it owns hardware-class detection, the disk gate, the
// pinned downloads (sha256-verified before unpack, always), the service
// install (systemd on Linux, WinSW on Windows — both must survive a reboot
// with nobody logged in, which is the whole point), the llama-swap config, the
// api key, and the second device row (<host>-llm at scope generate).
//
// THE PINS ARE EMBEDDED, not fetched: scripts/gen-local-manifest.js writes the
// manifest between the markers below, so the one file a machine installs
// carries its own pins and a runtime or model bump is by construction a
// reviewed cli-v* release. The named failure mode this prevents: a routine
// upstream patch silently degrading a GPU box to CPU with no error.
//
// WHAT ACTIVATION REFUSES TO AUTOMATE (detect and instruct, never bundle):
// GPU drivers (vendor EULA + admin + reboot), anything needing a reboot,
// exposing any port beyond loopback, and third-party runtimes whose terms
// forbid redistribution — adapter mode WRAPS an existing Ollama/LM Studio, it
// never installs one.
//
// Failure discipline: every step reports individually; a failing step stops
// the sequence and says what was done and what was not. `off` never claims
// what it did not do. Nothing here prints "removed" over a failure.

